7998,2,69,52,3,20,[0,5,20],[[31,"a",[2,1]]]],[0.8021,2,79,46,0,23,[0,5,23],[[31,"a",[2,1]]]],[0.813,2,216,39,1,35,[1,9,34],[[31,"a",[2,1]],[85,"a",[0]]]],[0.8192,2,90,56,0,26,[1,8,25],[[31,"a",[2,1]],[104,"a",[0]]]],[0.8215,2,75,44,2,23,[1,4,22],[[31,"a",[2,1]],[95,"d",[0]]]],[0.8319,2,299,57,1,63,[3,12,59],[[417,"a",[2]],[114,"a",[0]],[31,"a",[1]]]],[0.834,2,103,50,0,31,[3,6,28],[[31,"a",[2,1]],[104,"a",[0]]]],[0.8361,2,195,63,6,44,[3,9,41],[[31,"a",[2,1]],[210,"a",[0]]]],[0.8365,2,129,41,0,35,[1,6,34],[[31,"a",[2,1]],[95,"d",[0]]]],[0.8835,2,137,43,0,34,[1,9,33],[[31,"a",[2,1]],[111,"a",[0]]]],[0.906,2,117,26,1,31,[0,5,31],[[31,"a",[2,1]]]],[0.9192,2,325,52,0,68,[2,10,65],[[417,"a",[2]],[79,"a",[0]],[31,"a",[1]]]],[0.9258,2,251,55,0,65,[0,10,64],[[417,"a",[2]],[31,"a",[1]]]],[0.9539,2,300,45,1,71,[0,11,70],[[417,"a",[2]],[31,"a",[1]]]],[0.9548,2,328,51,6,71,[3,9,68],[[417,"a",[2]],[402,"a",[0]],[3,"a",[1]]]],[0.9852,2,174,43,0,37,[0,7,37],[[31,"a",[2,1]]]],[1.0,2,215,47,0,46,[0,10,46],[[31,"a",[2,1]]]]],"texts":{"3":"For me, trust comes down to the numbers: too many people have arrived too quickly for our communities to keep up.","8":"Migration keeps my workplace and my community going. Cutting it back would cost us more than it would save.","22":"Migration is about people, not just workers. Families being able to live together should count as much as economic contribution.","27":"If we expect newcomers to learn English, classes and settlement support should be funded for everyone, not just permanent arrivals.","31":"The culture of my community is changing faster than people can adjust, and it's fair to worry about that.","34":"As a lucky country, we have a duty to keep helping people who aren't so lucky, even when it costs us.","39":"Reducing migrant discourse solely to whether they use finite resources or can contribute via their labour reduces their humanity","40":"People would be less racist and more trusting of immigrants if they knew how badly Australia needs some of the skills - facts and numbers.","41":"Migration debates are often a thinly veiled excuse to indulge in racism","42":"There is nothing wrong with our immigration system. We are a migrant nation and economically dependent upon migration.","43":"This whole discussion is contrived by the hard right for political division. It's a repeat of their tactics in the Voice referendum.","44":"Politic is driving this discussion and creating unnecessary division. Let's celebrate our multicultural nation.","45":"We have a responsibility to welcome and offer refuge to asylum seekers and refugees. We take only 20,000 per year that's abysmal.","47":"The real question is, are we a generous and open society or selfish, greedy and xenophobic creating excuses to question immigration.","49":"For political representatives, decency, what's right, fair and generous (humanist) must be how you respond even if your electors disagree.","51":"Migrants make an outsized contribution to the community because they tend to be highly motivated and entrepreneurial by necessity","52":"There should be no bias towards any particular country of origin in migrant qualification criteria","55":"The only way to make housing more affordable is to build more and outstrip demand, and that requires bringing in more people to build homes","78":"Immigration should be discriminatory. We should only take the best.","79":"A bigger Australia is a richer Australia with more employers, workers, wealth and resources for all","83":"There is already plenty of factual information about how migration works, people choose to ignore it because they'd prefer to blame migrants","85":"Migration debate can often be centred around xenophobia and racism, which is not helpful.","95":"It's not the number of migrants that's the issue, it's cohesion. Will they assimilate and speak our common language, or form ghettos?","98":"Some of the recent immigration debate is just thinly disguised racism","104":"Migration plays an unacknowledged but important role in supporting economic growth (which safeguards against recession)","111":"Grandparents are waiting 10+ yrs for a visa.Given the shortage of childcare workers, it's a headwind to productivity, not to let them in.","114":"It needs to be much easier to get qualifications recognised from overseas in Australia.","131":"Hostility towards migrants stems from a one-size-fits all expectation of how migrants should act and what they look like","132":"We should focus on building trust and unity across communities rather than simply cutting migration.","173":"more stories would help us to understand what it is to be a migrant","177":"Australia is too lax on who can gain permanent residency / citizenship.","189":"I struggle with the protests on our streets where immigrants bring their mother country issues into our political realm.","197":"Migrant work ethic is what has built this nation since 1788.  Give us the tools and the knowledge and it will happen.","199":"The truth is new businesses start via migrants and most people forget this is helpful to the ecomony","210":"Unless you are indigenous, your ancestors were ALL migrants, so let's welcome newcomers to our lucky country","214":"We should welcome skilled migrants only if they are already sponsored by an employer.","217":"Most of the cultural or social concerns about migration would be alleviated by a smaller, slower migration program (100k)","279":"Migration is essential BUT quantity & quality are essential.At the moment quantity is too high & quality is mixed. Controls are required.","294":"We should be selecting migrants based on both their proven skills and countries with a high cultural and religious integration success rate.","299":"Migration is an economic imperative with a declining fertility rate and an ageing population.","308":"I have struggled to see the changes in our local area. Diversity is good but it now feels as though migrants are the majority.","313":"The governments cap of student visas not only damages the university sector, but students also pay rent, tax and do jobs others will not do.","329":"My son is denied work, any entry level, retail job he applies. No chance because only hire Asian or South Asian. Migration takes away jobs.","385":"We dont need more regulation, or programs. The individual needs to do their own work to learn English.","392":"I feel like a foreigner in my own home. There are too many communities not assimilating. Mass immigration does not allow integration.","402":"We would have more housing for migrants and residents if we taxed corporations and wealth more and built more government housing.","414":"New migrants do not have any affinity or bond with our history and thus no value is placed on heritage homes and places.","415":"There are only so many marbles one can fit into a jar before it is full. Our country can only support a finite number of people. We are full","416":"As a comparatively wealthy country we have a strong obligation to take in and support a wholesome number of true refugees","417":"Why does our Government think a Big Australia Policy is a good idea?  Zero migration during Covid did not hurt Australia.","426":"Migrants and their Australian born offspring from certain cultures account for disproportionately high crime and terrorism offences","452":"Immigration levels have been too high leading to stress on services and the housing crisis.","453":"We have allowed too many elderly immigrants on family reunion visas that are not contributing to the economy or integrating with community."},"nsplit":71}</script>
